        {
          "path": "_m/f/2/4/4/lebreton-flats-wp/plaque-on-the-fleet-st-pumping.jpg",
          "filename": "Plaque on the Fleet St. Pumping Station (20564488450).jpg",
          "caption": "The Fleet St. Pumping Station (which I'd initially thought to be the Ottawa Waterworks) had a tablet on it, which said 'Expanded 1888'. The sign is fairlyself explanatory if viewed in full screen mode. The Fleet Street Pumping Station was built for the Ottawa Water Works in 1874-75, for both fire suppression and domestic water supply. It was enlarged in 1888 and again in 1901.(Ottawa, Canada, June 2015)",
          "alt": "The Fleet St. Pumping Station (which I'd initially thought to be the Ottawa Waterworks) had a tablet on it, which said 'Expanded 1888'. The sign is fairlyself explanatory if viewed in full screen mode. The Fleet Street Pumping Station was built for the Ottawa Water Works in 1874-75, for both fire suppression and domestic water supply. It was enlarged in 1888 and again in 1901.(Ottawa, Canada, June 2015)",
          "width": 4288,
          "height": 2848,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
